    ("__main__ guard", "`if __name__ == '__main__':` separates importable logic from script entry — every module stays reusable."),
    ("__init__ packages", "`__init__.py` marks packages (implicit namespaces since 3.3 need none); relative imports (`.sibling`) stay internal."),
    ("PYTHONPATH pitfalls", "`PYTHONPATH` shims break reproducibility across machines — venvs + installs replace it in real projects."),
    ("-m execution", "`python -m pkg.mod` runs with package context (relative imports work); script paths don't — always `-m` in projects."),
    ("-O optimize asserts", "`python -O` strips asserts and `__debug__` blocks — never gate production logic on assert."),
